o.\n\nReason: The move e2-e4 is optimal because it maximizes central control, opens lines for the queen and bishop, and aligns with classical opening principles. It takes full advantage of the first-move privilege and is statistically one of the most winning-opening moves at all levels.\n\nAnswer: P: e2-e4"}
