ally strong move is **P: e4-e5**, which seizes the initiative by expanding in the center, limits Black’s counterplay, and prepares for rapid development of my dark-squared bishop and queen along open lines.\n\nReason: Advancing e4-e5 maximizes central control, disrupts Black’s coordination, and creates immediate pressure. It’s a tempo-gaining move that fits perfectly with White’s opening principles — control the center, develop with threats.\n\nAnswer: P: e4-e5"}
