ng check and exploiting the exposed black king.\n\nThis aligns with principles: attack the weakest point — the king.\n\nReason: The black king on f5 is abnormally exposed in the opening/middlegame. By playing N: e4-d6, White delivers check, forcing Black into a difficult response (either losing material or further weakening the king’s position). This move increases pressure, activates a key piece, and capitalizes on Black’s lack of development and king safety.\n\nAnswer: N: e4-d6'}
