 is in the valid move list: "N: e4-d6"\n\nYes.\n\nOther moves like P: a2-a4 or developing pawns are too slow given the tactical opportunity.\n\nReason: The black king is dangerously exposed on e5, and the knight fork **N: e4-d6** delivers check while simultaneously threatening the rook on f8. After the forced king move (likely Ke6), White captures the rook with Nxf8, gaining a full piece (rook vs knight). This significantly increases White’s material advantage and strengthens the attack. Other moves fail to capitalize on this fleeting tactical chance.\n\nAnswer: N: e4-d6'}
