o material gain or mate.\n- B: c6-e4: Also checks, but bishop can be captured by king — losing material for no gain — inferior.\n- N: f7-e5: Central outpost, but not forcing — allows king to consolidate — less effective.\n- Other pawn moves: Too slow for such a tactical position.\n\nReason: The black king is extremely exposed on f5, and the knight fork to d6 delivers a non-replicable check that cannot be parried by capture, forcing the king into a vulnerable retreat while maintaining initiative and threat of further attacks.\n\nAnswer: N: f7-d6'}
