ts Ng4, but not urgent.\n\nBest candidate: **R: e5-c5** — captures a pawn and attacks the black queen immediately, gaining material or forcing positional concessions.\n\nReason: Rxc5 wins a pawn and threatens the black queen. Even if Black saves the queen, we’ve gained material and disrupted their position. The rook is active and safe on c5. This move maximizes pressure and capitalizes on the exposed black queen.\n\nAnswer: R: e5-c5'}
