: f3-g4 – Captures the black queen! This is a free piece capture: QBF1 on g4 can be taken by PWF1 on f3 via f3xg4. This is highly advantageous.\n- P: f3-f4 – Pushes the pawn forward, closing the diagonal and potentially challenging the queen, but allows the queen to escape or reposition.\n- P: h2-h3 – Defensive move, preventing Qg4-h4+ or Qg4-g3+ checks by supporting g3; solid but passive.\n\nThe most promising move is **P: f3-g4**, capturing the undefended black queen. The black queen on g4 is completely unprotected — there are no black pieces defending it, and after Pxg4, Black loses their most powerful piece. This is a massive material gain (queen for a pawn), effectively deciding the game in White’s favor.\n\nReason: Capturing the undefended queen with P: f3-g4 is a winning move. It exploits a blunder by Black and gives White an overwhelming advantage. No other move comes close in evaluation.\n\nAnswer: P: f3-g4'}
