-g6-f5-e4-d3 → no.\n                    - Horizontal: queen on 7th rank → g7, not g4.\n                    - Vertical: h-file → h4, but not g4.\n                    → g4 not attacked.\n                → So black king can go to g3 or g4.\n\n        Therefore, Qh7+ is **not** checkmate — black escapes.\n\n    But wait — what about Qg7-h8? That\'s also an option.\n\n    Try Qg7-h8:\n    - Queen on h8: controls h-file (h1–h8), 8th rank, and diagonal h8-a1 (same as before).\n    - Attacks h3? Yes — vertically.\n    - So Qh8+ checks the king.\n\n    King moves:\n        - h3-g3: not attacked by queen? h8 to g3: not same file/rank/diagonal → safe.\n        - h3-g4: same — not attacked.\n    → Also not mate.\n\n    What about Qg7-c3? That’s a long-range move.\n\n    Qg7-c3: queen goes to c3.\n    - Does it attack h3? c3 to h3 is same rank? No — c3 is rank 3, h3 is rank 3 → same rank! Yes, rank 3.\n    - So queen on c3 attacks entire rank 3 — including h3 → check!\n\n    Is it checkmate?\n\n    After Qc3+, black king on h3:\n        - Possible moves:\n            - h3-g3: g3 is on rank 3 — queen on c3 attacks g3 → still in check.\n            - h3-h2: h2 — is it attacked? Queen on c3 attacks h2? Same file? No. Same rank? No (h2 is rank 2). Diagonal? c3 to h2: c3-d2-e1 → no. Δfile=5, Δrank=1 → not diagonal. → h2 not attacked.\n            → So king can escape to h2.\n\n        So not mate.\n\n    What about Qg7-g3+? That’s not in the list — g3 is occupied? No, g3 is empty. But is Q: g7-g3 in the valid moves? Looking at list:\n\n    Valid moves: Q: g7-g3 — YES, it is listed.\n\n    Qg7-g3: queen moves to g3 — same file as g7, so vertical move. g3 is on same file? g7 to g3 → yes, along g-file.\n\n    Now, queen on g3:\n        - Controls g-file: g1–g8\n        - Rank 3: a3–h3\n        - Diagonals: g3-f4-e5-d6-c7-b8 and g3-f2-e1\n\n    Now, king on h3:\n        - Adjacent squares:\n            - h3-g3: occupied by queen → blocked\n            - h3-h2: attacked? Queen on g3 attacks h2? Diagonal: g3-f2-e1 → no. g3 to h2: one right, one down → yes! g3→h2 is +1 file, -1 rank → diagonal → yes, queen attacks h2.\n            - h3-h4: same file → queen on g3 does **not** control h4 (different file, different rank, not diagonal: g3 to h4 is +1, +1 → yes! +1 file, +1 rank → diagonal → yes, h4 is attacked.\n            - h3-g4: g4 — is it attacked? g3 to g4 is same file → yes, queen controls g4 (g-file).\n            - h3-g2: g2 — same file → yes, controlled.\n\n        So all surrounding squares:\n            - g3: occupied by queen\n            - g4: attacked\n            - h4: attacked (diagonal)\n            - g2: attacked (g-file)\n            - h2: attacked (diagonal)\n\n        And king is on h3, which is under attack by queen on g3? Is h3 attacked?\n\n        Queen on g3 to h3: same rank? g3 and h3 are both rank 3 → yes! So queen attacks entire rank 3 → h3 is attacked → **check**.\n\n        So black king is in check, and all escape squares are either occupied or attacked → **checkmate**.\n\n    But is Qg7-g3 in the move list? Yes: "Q: g7-g3" is explicitly listed.\n\n    Therefore, **Qg7-g3** delivers checkmate.\n\nReason: Qg7-g3 places the queen on g3, delivering check to the black king on h3 along the third rank. All adjacent escape squares (g2, g3, g4, h2, h4) are either occupied by the queen or attacked by it (via rank, file, or diagonal), leaving the black king with no legal moves — resulting in checkmate.\n\nAnswer: Q: g7-g3'}
